    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nPossibly related: #13821\n\nI've installed nvim on macos through Homebrew. In 0.12.3, I noticed that deleting lines in a split caused a different buffer the next left split to apparently have deleted the same lines wholesale. The left buffer had not actually changed, and refreshed correctly. 0.12.4 and nightly both show a somewhat different behavior that still mangles splits to the left.\n\nGiven two splits, with `-u NORC`:\n\n<img width=\"672\" height=\"428\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9dceae31-a273-49ac-abfd-6c9840413299\" />\n\nDelete one or more lines in the right-side split (here, I've deleted the \"Clear an argument list\" comment):\n\n<img width=\"672\" height=\"428\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/415477a0-923e-48cc-b9de-b31906aef9b3\" />\n\nUndoing deletes characters from the split divider (!):\n\n<img width=\"672\" height=\"428\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d17172ab-ab58-4da5-bc3c-216d0f3491d7\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a vertical split and bring up two files.\n2. Delete one or more lines in the _right_ file.\n3. The left buffer appears mangled.\n4. Undo the action.\n5. Characters in the split divider are erased.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nDeleting lines has no apparent side effects in other visible interface elements.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4 LuaJIT 2.1.1782726002; also NVIM v0.13.0-dev-934+g6a6431cb99\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nhaven't checked\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacos tahoe 26.5.2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew",
